1
00:00:04,026 --> 00:00:18,838
[SPEAKER_01]: The experience of an other, of another person, your experience of another, as I said, it's true, it's correct to say, oh yes, that's the experience of your five aggregates.

2
00:00:20,079 --> 00:00:32,128
[SPEAKER_01]: But if that experience of another is not seen as an image correctly, independent of space and time, if that phenomenon is not seen peripherally,

3
00:00:33,442 --> 00:00:42,789
[SPEAKER_01]: It will imply that there is also the internal experience of others and their counterpart that you are not privy to.

4
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:46,151
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's already outside of your aggregate assumption.

5
00:00:46,692 --> 00:00:49,954
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why self exists internally or externally for that matter.

6
00:00:52,055 --> 00:00:55,318
[SPEAKER_01]: So the self will... the sense of self or the conceit

7
00:00:56,535 --> 00:01:11,582
[SPEAKER_01]: For a putuja, for an Arya Sāvaka, who is free from ātavāda, but he still is not free from his self-centeredness, to varying, various degrees, that also implies a certain perception of private self-centeredness of others.

8
00:01:13,343 --> 00:01:17,885
[SPEAKER_01]: Private conceit, that he's not, as I said, that he cannot access, but it's there.

9
00:01:18,346 --> 00:01:21,167
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, if he starts seeing that as an image,

10
00:01:24,283 --> 00:01:26,924
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how the emphasis gets undone.

11
00:01:26,984 --> 00:01:32,907
[SPEAKER_01]: The image remains the same, the phenomenon remains the same, the designation remains the same, but what it implies changes.

12
00:01:35,828 --> 00:01:36,809
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's important.

13
00:01:37,849 --> 00:01:39,330
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, as a practice, obviously.

14
00:01:40,319 --> 00:01:42,980
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you do it like that, then... See, if like...

15
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:50,861
[SPEAKER_01]: If somebody, who is still very much assumes the internal of their experience here and now, you know, is mine, and...

16
00:01:50,901 --> 00:01:54,882
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter whether they take scientific view, or mystical view, or whatever.

17
00:01:55,062 --> 00:01:56,263
[SPEAKER_01]: If they're seeing...

18
00:01:56,363 --> 00:01:57,683
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't act out of others still there.

19
00:01:58,103 --> 00:02:05,345
[SPEAKER_01]: When you tell them that experience of another is just an image, they're gonna assume, aha, so others are just in me.

20
00:02:06,457 --> 00:02:10,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Here, right here, in this space and time of me.

21
00:02:11,398 --> 00:02:12,518
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's like solipsism.

22
00:02:13,858 --> 00:02:22,520
[SPEAKER_01]: But, the dhamma I've done rightly, others are not in you more than you are in them, from your point of view.

23
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:35,062
[SPEAKER_01]: So, in other words, when you cease to be self for yourself here, to that extent, other selves out there will also cease to be selves.

24
00:02:36,718 --> 00:02:39,039
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not just that others are not in you.

25
00:02:39,380 --> 00:02:42,342
[SPEAKER_01]: Even you is not in you.

26
00:02:42,362 --> 00:02:54,249
[SPEAKER_01]: But, obviously, somebody who is still on the level of me, here, sense of self, attavāda, anything, any information like this, they will not see the nuance difference and they will just... it just sounds like solipsism.

27
00:02:54,289 --> 00:02:55,910
[SPEAKER_01]: It just sounds like everybody is in me.

28
00:02:56,170 --> 00:02:57,651
[SPEAKER_01]: My perception is what everybody is.

29
00:02:58,011 --> 00:02:59,152
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no real everybody.

30
00:02:59,172 --> 00:03:00,173
[SPEAKER_01]: This is only what I perceive.

31
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:00,733
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like...

32
00:03:00,913 --> 00:03:03,755
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's undermined by the sense of self assuming internally.

33
00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:09,051
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you were to approve that, they will cease to be in you, so to speak.

34
00:03:09,491 --> 00:03:15,353
[SPEAKER_01]: They will be neither here nor there, nor between the two, as actually Bhagavad-Gītā says.

35
00:03:15,373 --> 00:03:15,873
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

36
00:03:17,134 --> 00:03:24,696
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why if, like, in case of an arahant, as I said, that's where his confidence comes from.

37
00:03:26,517 --> 00:03:29,458
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why he doesn't tremble amidst any of assembly.

38
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:45,598
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because he's not percipient that there are many people around him, but it's because one or thousand people, there are no assumed, private, internal dimension that has a view of me that I cannot access.

39
00:03:46,618 --> 00:03:49,581
[SPEAKER_01]: That which undermines my sense of me, gone.

40
00:03:50,241 --> 00:03:53,044
[SPEAKER_01]: He sees that as a peripheral image, neither here nor there.

41
00:03:53,584 --> 00:04:02,052
[SPEAKER_01]: If he thinks about his own self-centeredness in regard to others, he thinks about that as a peripheral image, neither here nor there, as a phenomenon, independent of space or time.

42
00:04:02,552 --> 00:04:10,179
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there can be no more fear towards others, no more anger towards others, no more lusting after others, and

43
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:15,841
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, when we started talking, you could see that's exactly... you could... you could even imagine that.

44
00:04:15,881 --> 00:04:17,761
[SPEAKER_01]: You could get a... you could get a taste of that.

45
00:04:18,281 --> 00:04:26,583
[SPEAKER_01]: How to live... like, imagine you live in a crowded home, where... where everything... everything is, like, seen.

46
00:04:27,823 --> 00:04:34,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything you do, everything you say is constantly, basically, paired with... with eyes of others and company.

47
00:04:36,388 --> 00:04:49,618
[SPEAKER_01]: And thoughts, and so on, and all of that carries that external point of view to me, that I don't have control of, and that's why I feel undermined, and shy, or irritated, or just just tired, or whatever.

48
00:04:49,738 --> 00:04:59,825
[SPEAKER_01]: And imagine now, they all disappear, and you just feel alone, and you're gonna feel relief, because it's just you with yourself, to the extent that you are.

49
00:05:01,273 --> 00:05:02,013
[SPEAKER_01]: No more, no less.

50
00:05:02,394 --> 00:05:05,676
[SPEAKER_01]: And then just sit and put your feet up, and you just feel nice.

51
00:05:05,756 --> 00:05:14,201
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there is nobody there, just having their input, having their presence of that external kind, that fundamentally it's unpleasant.

52
00:05:14,902 --> 00:05:17,583
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what Laksātra was describing, the being for others.

53
00:05:17,704 --> 00:05:19,184
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's always out of my hand.

54
00:05:19,204 --> 00:05:21,266
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why my being... How do you put it?

55
00:05:21,766 --> 00:05:22,987
[SPEAKER_01]: My being kind of...

56
00:05:24,293 --> 00:05:28,974
[SPEAKER_01]: It gets taken from me, in a sense, into that dimension, and you feel that, but you're not saying it.

57
00:05:29,295 --> 00:05:33,496
[SPEAKER_01]: There's a nice, poetic, almost, description of the fact, but he couldn't see the way out.

58
00:05:34,156 --> 00:05:42,239
[SPEAKER_01]: But the way out is, that which you assume is there, outside the internal dimension, is another phenomenon.

59
00:05:42,499 --> 00:05:46,080
[SPEAKER_01]: Another phenomenon, another image, another dhamma, independent of space and time.

60
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:52,322
[SPEAKER_01]: That which you assume as the internal, behind all these senses, in me, same.

61
00:05:53,291 --> 00:05:56,253
[SPEAKER_01]: So, contemplate things internally, contemplate things externally.

62
00:05:56,373 --> 00:06:05,157
[SPEAKER_01]: There will be no room for self to hide, because self requires that internal dimension, assumed implication.

63
00:06:05,558 --> 00:06:09,880
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether that dimension is at the counterpart of me or others, it doesn't matter.

64
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,421
[SPEAKER_00]: It's external to the experience as a whole.

65
00:06:16,403 --> 00:06:22,947
[SPEAKER_01]: So, people, animals, brahmas, devas, maras, for an arhant,

66
00:06:24,094 --> 00:06:36,226
[SPEAKER_01]: No internal dimension assumed, that is outside of him, given footing to exist through his... through his misconception of his images, in regard to those things.

67
00:06:36,306 --> 00:06:39,509
[SPEAKER_01]: It's all seen for what it is, and that's why he's unshakable.

68
00:06:41,055 --> 00:06:42,996
[SPEAKER_00]: So, not misconceiving images.

69
00:06:43,256 --> 00:06:43,476
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

70
00:06:44,397 --> 00:06:46,338
[SPEAKER_00]: Imaging, imaging, imaging.

71
00:06:46,478 --> 00:06:55,444
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, but images, as I said, images is what you find at the back of your mind in regard to things, not what you kind of think, oh, this is an image of it.

72
00:06:57,985 --> 00:06:58,826
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

73
00:06:59,026 --> 00:07:00,767
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, discerning images.

74
00:07:05,210 --> 00:07:05,630
[SPEAKER_00]: As images.

75
00:07:06,252 --> 00:07:08,013
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, discerning image is image.

76
00:07:08,293 --> 00:07:14,716
[SPEAKER_01]: As we spoke in the other recent talk, the group talk we had here, it's like, so do you think images are in your head?

77
00:07:16,297 --> 00:07:21,020
[SPEAKER_01]: And usually, that's usually the first thing people will be thinking, which means that's the first thing you have to start undoing.

78
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:31,625
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when images cease to be in your head, images of others, that imply their personal, their being, independent of you, will cease to be placed in them.

79
00:07:32,365 --> 00:07:34,246
[SPEAKER_01]: It will be seen as a phenomenon.

80
00:07:34,266 --> 00:07:35,227
[SPEAKER_01]: It's neither here nor there.

81
00:07:36,672 --> 00:07:40,434
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, neither here nor there is quite a good picture.

82
00:07:40,754 --> 00:07:45,756
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, yeah, non-locality... Yeah, so you could see, like, the practicality of Bhagya Sutta.

83
00:07:46,957 --> 00:07:55,561
[SPEAKER_01]: He was not just, like, a philosophical statement, or a logical, hey, let me, let me provide you a system of seen and heard, and how it connects all the dots.

84
00:07:55,721 --> 00:07:55,881
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

85
00:07:56,801 --> 00:08:00,803
[SPEAKER_01]: You see it like that rightly, you will be neither here nor there, nor between the two.

86
00:08:00,823 --> 00:08:04,645
[SPEAKER_01]: Nor anybody will be anything neither there nor here, nor between the two.

87
00:08:09,250 --> 00:08:10,111
[SPEAKER_01]: And he was an arahant.

88
00:08:15,134 --> 00:08:16,114
[SPEAKER_01]: Simply on account of that.

89
00:08:16,895 --> 00:08:17,715
[SPEAKER_01]: Understanding that.

90
00:08:20,457 --> 00:08:26,641
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, it sounds, you know, like this room is empty of self.

91
00:08:27,561 --> 00:08:29,162
[SPEAKER_00]: This place is empty of self.

92
00:08:29,262 --> 00:08:30,423
[SPEAKER_00]: Anything pertaining to self.

93
00:08:31,564 --> 00:08:35,426
[SPEAKER_00]: It sounds like he enters into that emptiness.

94
00:08:37,507 --> 00:08:38,788
[SPEAKER_00]: Or there's nothing

95
00:08:41,390 --> 00:08:44,272
[SPEAKER_00]: There's nothing belonging to me anywhere.

96
00:08:44,893 --> 00:08:47,074
[SPEAKER_01]: Anywhere in the world, yeah, yeah, exactly.

97
00:08:47,354 --> 00:08:48,916
[SPEAKER_00]: It's basically the same kind of...

98
00:08:48,996 --> 00:08:52,898
[SPEAKER_01]: It's exactly, yeah, it paints the same, it sets up the same...

99
00:08:53,439 --> 00:08:53,819
[SPEAKER_00]: Images.

100
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,261
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, images, contemplation.

101
00:08:56,281 --> 00:08:58,942
[SPEAKER_01]: It sets up the same sort of recognition.

102
00:09:00,524 --> 00:09:06,848
[SPEAKER_01]: That then, you need to, as I said, sustain and maintain

103
00:09:07,755 --> 00:09:12,879
[SPEAKER_01]: In the sense of... until it permeates all the subtle aspects.

104
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,722
[SPEAKER_01]: All the subtler implications.

105
00:09:17,922 --> 00:09:19,303
[SPEAKER_01]: Subtler images.

106
00:09:20,864 --> 00:09:23,306
[SPEAKER_00]: Where are others for you now?

107
00:09:23,646 --> 00:09:24,366
[SPEAKER_00]: Where's your mother?

108
00:09:24,447 --> 00:09:25,227
[SPEAKER_00]: Where's your father?

109
00:09:25,307 --> 00:09:25,507
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

110
00:09:25,887 --> 00:09:27,008
[SPEAKER_01]: You look at the dog now.

111
00:09:27,068 --> 00:09:28,229
[SPEAKER_01]: Jabu, where is he now?

112
00:09:28,429 --> 00:09:33,092
[SPEAKER_01]: Is he in that lamp of flesh, you know, coated with a fur blanket?

113
00:09:33,193 --> 00:09:34,674
[SPEAKER_01]: Is he inside there?

114
00:09:35,814 --> 00:09:36,635
[SPEAKER_01]: Why would you assume that?

115
00:09:37,847 --> 00:09:39,388
[SPEAKER_01]: Also, is he in need then?

116
00:09:39,428 --> 00:09:45,590
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize all these thoughts means you still give priority to he is somewhere and you don't see that as an image.

117
00:09:48,411 --> 00:09:54,013
[SPEAKER_01]: And the point is, you can't see it as an image once or twice for that assumption to drain away.

118
00:09:54,834 --> 00:09:55,794
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to keep seeing it.

119
00:09:56,214 --> 00:09:59,876
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to keep catching yourself each time, which means you need to have faith in the instruction.

120
00:10:00,848 --> 00:10:05,231
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you don't have faith in the instruction, I tell you, you look at it once and you don't see it as an image.

121
00:10:05,491 --> 00:10:06,832
[SPEAKER_01]: I see it as has to be somewhere.

122
00:10:06,872 --> 00:10:07,813
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, it's a fact.

123
00:10:08,394 --> 00:10:10,015
[SPEAKER_01]: How can he be here if he's not somewhere?

124
00:10:10,055 --> 00:10:12,096
[SPEAKER_01]: How can... What am I perceiving if he's not somewhere?

125
00:10:13,157 --> 00:10:14,078
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you're going to dismiss it.

126
00:10:14,538 --> 00:10:19,402
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you repeat it a sufficient amount of times, seeing it as an image, you recognize, oh, crap, it is an image.

127
00:10:21,283 --> 00:10:23,865
[SPEAKER_01]: Independent of space and time, it's not in me, it's not in him.

128
00:10:25,306 --> 00:10:25,847
[SPEAKER_01]: It's there.

129
00:10:27,167 --> 00:10:27,628
[SPEAKER_00]: Likewise.

130
00:10:28,404 --> 00:10:31,545
[SPEAKER_01]: Likewise, anything that has a nature to appear.

131
00:10:33,565 --> 00:10:33,985
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything.

132
00:10:34,385 --> 00:10:34,785
[SPEAKER_01]: Anything.

133
00:10:36,646 --> 00:10:40,007
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when it ceases to be here and yonder and between the two.

134
00:10:41,387 --> 00:10:48,788
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, like, so sensuality, sensual pleasure is in the object of the senses.

135
00:10:50,149 --> 00:10:51,289
[SPEAKER_00]: That's where it is.

136
00:10:51,329 --> 00:10:56,190
[SPEAKER_00]: If I just go towards it, then I get it from there into here.

137
00:10:57,008 --> 00:10:57,989
[SPEAKER_00]: Out there, into here.

138
00:10:58,169 --> 00:10:58,870
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, of course.

139
00:10:58,990 --> 00:11:00,051
[SPEAKER_01]: It requires that division.

140
00:11:00,751 --> 00:11:09,858
[SPEAKER_01]: But the whole idea, like, whatever it is... Well, the whole idea, like, see, you're not seeing that when you are thinking about the central object, that is already the extent of the central object.

141
00:11:10,698 --> 00:11:13,741
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, why would you have subsequent actions towards it?

142
00:11:14,441 --> 00:11:15,422
[SPEAKER_00]: It's the gratification.

143
00:11:15,782 --> 00:11:20,406
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize, well, but it's the extent of it that it can be present, it's already present.

144
00:11:23,068 --> 00:11:24,669
[SPEAKER_01]: That is already its gratification.

145
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:31,416
[SPEAKER_01]: So, following things further with the body and so on, it's like, well, it's completely redundant.

146
00:11:32,597 --> 00:11:33,417
[SPEAKER_00]: That makes no sense.

147
00:11:35,859 --> 00:11:48,967
[SPEAKER_01]: That requires you to not see it as an image to the extent that it has a reason, and then your actions seem to be gaining and fulfilling and consuming the lack, what was missing.

148
00:11:51,028 --> 00:11:55,851
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you see what's missing as an image, you realize, well, delighting in what's missing,

149
00:11:56,826 --> 00:11:58,086
[SPEAKER_00]: As an image, it's really such.

150
00:12:00,687 --> 00:12:16,493
[SPEAKER_01]: Missing is complete, so to speak, as an image, independent of space and time, and then it stops to imply the missing, the lack, which means your delight fades away.

151
00:12:17,913 --> 00:12:22,475
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not incidental that anāgāmī

152
00:12:24,504 --> 00:12:29,325
[SPEAKER_01]: is free from sensuality and ill-will.

153
00:12:29,345 --> 00:12:43,148
[SPEAKER_01]: Because both require that extent of the implication of another, of that dimension that you're getting to through pursuing pleasure or expressing anger.

154
00:12:44,248 --> 00:12:51,750
[SPEAKER_01]: But when that's seen real as such to the extent that it has a reason, it has no no lack in itself,

155
00:12:52,572 --> 00:13:01,299
[SPEAKER_01]: And that scene, sufficiently and repeatedly, as I said, any actions, any assumptions that exist on account of that assumed lack, will disappear.

156
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,421
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you will not be able to get angry.

157
00:13:05,762 --> 00:13:15,410
[SPEAKER_01]: You will not be able to get lustful and drawn towards the attractive form.

158
00:13:20,256 --> 00:13:22,499
[SPEAKER_01]: It requires personification, basically.

159
00:13:22,739 --> 00:13:26,184
[SPEAKER_00]: Those actions require you to personify the form that you perceive.

160
00:13:27,025 --> 00:13:27,566
[SPEAKER_01]: Which you are.

161
00:13:27,846 --> 00:13:29,148
[SPEAKER_01]: You start with personification.

162
00:13:29,168 --> 00:13:31,732
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't start clean and then make a mistake.

163
00:13:50,797 --> 00:14:10,331
[SPEAKER_01]: And when the form is de-personified, here and yonder, immediately, reflexively, doesn't matter, when form is... was basically... when image of form is seen as an image understood to its extent, there can be no disturbances arising in you.

164
00:14:11,612 --> 00:14:16,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Because any disturbance that comes, requires self, internally or externally, or both.

165
00:14:20,503 --> 00:14:43,120
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, the fear, lust, desire, loneliness, depression, any of these feelings and sort of complex dukkhas and so on, it's all in relation to others or seeing yourself as a self.

166
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:48,581
[SPEAKER_00]: Internal and external spaces, private spaces.

167
00:14:48,621 --> 00:14:50,101
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly, private spaces, yeah.

168
00:14:54,282 --> 00:15:04,545
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why Arahant, he said, for him, his actions, or his entire being, is as in private, so in public, as in public, so in private.

169
00:15:04,665 --> 00:15:09,106
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely no discrepancy.

170
00:15:09,146 --> 00:15:10,286
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no privacy.

171
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:12,667
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no privacy, but there is no

172
00:15:13,866 --> 00:15:14,806
[SPEAKER_01]: There is no private space.

173
00:15:15,547 --> 00:15:19,288
[SPEAKER_01]: But see, that also means there is no public space either.

174
00:15:20,689 --> 00:15:24,490
[SPEAKER_01]: Because public space is basically private space of others that you are not privy to.

175
00:15:25,191 --> 00:15:30,633
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people fear the public, public speaking, exposure, public, everybody looking at me.

176
00:15:32,254 --> 00:15:33,214
[SPEAKER_01]: You're basically...

177
00:15:33,234 --> 00:15:34,775
[SPEAKER_01]: It brings down...

178
00:15:34,855 --> 00:15:42,158
[SPEAKER_01]: It reveals the gratuitously assumed dimension of outside of yourself that shows you your non-control.

179
00:15:42,883 --> 00:15:45,345
[SPEAKER_01]: But you're assuming it through your control and you don't see that.

180
00:15:45,485 --> 00:15:50,690
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the discrepancy felt when others are looking at you and you feel like put on spot.

181
00:15:57,356 --> 00:16:07,425
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not seeing the outside you're experiencing as an image independent of space and time, independent of inside and outside, of here and yonder.

182
00:16:11,328 --> 00:16:12,609
[SPEAKER_01]: And for that, you are responsible.

183
00:16:13,089 --> 00:16:19,675
[SPEAKER_01]: So, see, you are responsible for giving that gratuitous power to that phenomenon of outside point of view.

184
00:16:21,476 --> 00:16:22,577
[SPEAKER_01]: You're giving power to it.

185
00:16:23,798 --> 00:16:28,422
[SPEAKER_01]: But that phenomenon, it shows you that you have no power, because it can go either way.

186
00:16:29,062 --> 00:16:29,603
[SPEAKER_01]: And you know that.

187
00:16:35,587 --> 00:16:40,031
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's why, like, it feels like it's out of your hands, but it's your doing.

188
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:44,442
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you feel embarrassed.

189
00:16:44,482 --> 00:16:50,825
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if you didn't do anything wrong, just by everybody watching you, your hands start to tremble, you can't speak, all this, you're exposed.

190
00:16:52,206 --> 00:17:01,231
[SPEAKER_01]: It reveals the most deepest personal assumption in regard to you, yourself, that you have regarding yourself.

191
00:17:01,271 --> 00:17:06,735
[SPEAKER_01]: An outside point of view, that in regard to yourself, you feel protect and hidden on the inside of me.

192
00:17:07,775 --> 00:17:10,537
[SPEAKER_01]: But it just shows you that the same thing is out there.

193
00:17:11,882 --> 00:17:12,622
[SPEAKER_01]: In regard to others.

194
00:17:13,442 --> 00:17:17,463
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, it reveals the inside of you that you thought was safe, because it wasn't seen.

195
00:17:18,923 --> 00:17:19,824
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're not seeing it.

196
00:17:20,884 --> 00:17:22,944
[SPEAKER_01]: If you were to start seeing it, it would be vomited out.

197
00:17:23,524 --> 00:17:25,725
[SPEAKER_01]: It would be seen as an external phenomenon.

198
00:17:30,386 --> 00:17:38,007
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you think about, for example, your mother, she's absent from here, she's out there, she's in South Africa,

199
00:17:41,559 --> 00:17:43,440
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you recognize the extent of that thought.

200
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,680
[SPEAKER_01]: You can see, oh, that's a thought.

201
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:50,802
[SPEAKER_01]: But that thought still carries...

202
00:17:52,443 --> 00:18:04,307
[SPEAKER_01]: But that thought still carries, well, still implies that she is, a being of her, is out there in South Africa.

203
00:18:05,868 --> 00:18:06,708
[SPEAKER_01]: And how can you know that?

204
00:18:09,653 --> 00:18:15,716
[SPEAKER_01]: How can that implication be anything other than just another peripheral image, in regard to your thoughts of your mother?

205
00:18:15,736 --> 00:18:16,576
[SPEAKER_01]: Because she might not be there.

206
00:18:17,436 --> 00:18:21,798
[SPEAKER_01]: Her form might have been disintegrated with a nuclear blast, and you're about to find out.

207
00:18:22,979 --> 00:18:27,821
[SPEAKER_01]: So, she's factually might not be there, the way you're thinking she is there.

208
00:18:29,081 --> 00:18:30,222
[SPEAKER_01]: So, she's probably there.

209
00:18:31,703 --> 00:18:36,145
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like probability is all I can have, but probabilities are real as such.

210
00:18:36,705 --> 00:18:39,346
[SPEAKER_01]: But whether your probability now, that probability,

211
00:18:40,635 --> 00:18:46,318
[SPEAKER_01]: That implies the external space, the world where your mother lives.

212
00:18:47,799 --> 00:18:59,684
[SPEAKER_01]: But then again, that implication will be there, but you look at it peripherally and see, but that implication, when I'm thinking about my mother, is just another image.

213
00:18:59,704 --> 00:19:06,808
[SPEAKER_01]: That's sure, less direct, less defined, closer to my point of view, but again, it's manifested.

214
00:19:07,642 --> 00:19:10,544
[SPEAKER_01]: And whatever's manifested, it's neither here nor yonder.

215
00:19:14,067 --> 00:19:17,409
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a reason to the extent... it has a reason independent of space and time.

216
00:19:18,189 --> 00:19:19,310
[SPEAKER_01]: Space and time are second to it.

217
00:19:21,131 --> 00:19:22,252
[SPEAKER_01]: And as such, it's impermanent.

218
00:19:26,655 --> 00:19:33,380
[SPEAKER_01]: See, by undermining the external assumption of the world, the matter that your mother lives in, you're undermining your own as well.

219
00:19:36,096 --> 00:19:40,738
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why people would be afraid to do it, because you would feel it here and now as well.

220
00:19:49,460 --> 00:20:03,225
[SPEAKER_01]: So, colloquially described, see, that the peripheral thoughts, images of the possibilities, of this and that, doesn't matter, that appear real as such, that that domain,

221
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:08,383
[SPEAKER_01]: That's independent of space and time, neither here nor there, not in your head, not in others.

222
00:20:08,543 --> 00:20:22,792
[SPEAKER_01]: It just is, to the extent that it is, that it's more real than your concrete sense of being here, this body, perceptions that come on account of it.

223
00:20:24,093 --> 00:20:24,413
[SPEAKER_01]: All that.

224
00:20:24,873 --> 00:20:26,595
[SPEAKER_01]: And by more real, I mean more fundamental.

225
00:20:28,016 --> 00:20:28,556
[SPEAKER_01]: It's first.

226
00:20:29,817 --> 00:20:31,458
[SPEAKER_01]: Your concreteness here, that you

227
00:20:32,185 --> 00:20:35,888
[SPEAKER_01]: palpable, palpability of it, all that is second to it.

228
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:49,418
[SPEAKER_01]: So now it's like, okay, so this concreteness, take it up, feel that physicality, as I was saying, and see the phenomenality of it.

229
00:20:49,938 --> 00:20:54,001
[SPEAKER_00]: See the peripheral image of it while you're feeling it here and now.

230
00:20:54,641 --> 00:21:00,686
[SPEAKER_01]: And then recognize it's the peripheral image of it comes first, while the physicality is perceived here.

231
00:21:25,642 --> 00:21:32,125
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I'm experiencing something here now, doing this and that, drinking, someone speaking.

232
00:21:33,545 --> 00:21:40,528
[SPEAKER_00]: All that is secondary to the image of it, of the experience as a whole, in regard to all of those specifics.

233
00:21:42,229 --> 00:21:48,351
[SPEAKER_01]: But see, the image of the whole, the image of the experience as a whole, depends on the specifics.

234
00:21:52,622 --> 00:21:56,425
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's not just how you have these magical images and then everything else follows out of them.

235
00:21:56,825 --> 00:21:57,125
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no.

236
00:21:58,386 --> 00:21:59,266
[SPEAKER_01]: You have two domains.

237
00:22:00,387 --> 00:22:03,849
[SPEAKER_01]: Domains of the specifics and domains of the images of the experience as a whole.

238
00:22:05,150 --> 00:22:06,251
[SPEAKER_01]: The actual, the peripheral.

239
00:22:08,332 --> 00:22:10,094
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneously existing to the extent they are.

240
00:22:10,214 --> 00:22:12,475
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like looking at the same thing from two points of view.

241
00:22:16,478 --> 00:22:19,400
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, imagine, I don't know, again, it's a poor example because it's...

242
00:22:20,843 --> 00:22:24,344
[SPEAKER_01]: Even three-dimensional cannot convey the example, because it depends on space.

243
00:22:24,464 --> 00:22:49,870
[SPEAKER_01]: But, I think I might have said this before, like, I don't know, imagine your screen, your laptop screen, divided in half, and one is showing a view of the Earth, planet Earth, from the universe, from the space, and the other one is showing some view of a camera on the street.

244
00:22:50,945 --> 00:22:52,266
[SPEAKER_01]: Both are happening in real time.

245
00:22:57,589 --> 00:22:59,470
[SPEAKER_01]: Factually, both are happening in real time.

246
00:23:04,212 --> 00:23:09,455
[SPEAKER_01]: The events on the street are happening within that earth that's watched from the higher point of view.

247
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:11,196
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneous.

248
00:23:11,936 --> 00:23:15,258
[SPEAKER_01]: One doesn't stop in order for other to arise.

249
00:23:18,185 --> 00:23:21,788
[SPEAKER_01]: And by the way, that is actually decontemplation of the great elements.

250
00:23:22,649 --> 00:23:26,832
[SPEAKER_01]: How you undo your own little measly sense of personified form here.

251
00:23:28,434 --> 00:23:29,394
[SPEAKER_01]: By recognizing.

252
00:23:29,895 --> 00:23:35,880
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I established my mind upon the perception of Earth, so that anything inferior to it cannot bother me.

253
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:45,748
[SPEAKER_01]: See, if your concerns now shift onto the image on the screen that's basically planet Earth viewed from the space,

254
00:23:47,260 --> 00:23:51,002
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're concerned about what's gonna happen there, is there an asteroid coming and stuff?

255
00:23:51,703 --> 00:23:57,026
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything that's happening live, in real time, simultaneous on the street, it's completely irrelevant.

256
00:23:57,086 --> 00:24:02,769
[SPEAKER_01]: There was an argument over a pot of flowers between the neighbors or something.

257
00:24:03,950 --> 00:24:12,855
[SPEAKER_01]: There was like raging mad about to kill each other, but now suddenly your concern is on the level of the element of planet Earth.

258
00:24:14,176 --> 00:24:15,036
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneous still.

259
00:24:15,236 --> 00:24:16,157
[SPEAKER_01]: The argument didn't stop.

260
00:24:16,991 --> 00:24:19,473
[SPEAKER_01]: It just becomes irrelevant, because you see there's something bigger.

261
00:24:19,853 --> 00:24:22,295
[SPEAKER_01]: Possibilities of something bigger could occur.

262
00:24:24,277 --> 00:24:24,898
[SPEAKER_01]: And will occur.

263
00:24:25,658 --> 00:24:26,539
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the recognition.

264
00:24:26,699 --> 00:24:27,880
[SPEAKER_01]: It will break down.

265
00:24:28,761 --> 00:24:31,503
[SPEAKER_01]: So, everything here, simultaneous to that.

266
00:24:32,003 --> 00:24:40,230
[SPEAKER_01]: Not in hindsight, when I think about it, and convince myself that everything here is irrelevant, because the earth is greatest, and it will come to pass, and then... No, no, no.

267
00:24:40,290 --> 00:24:43,533
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneous, live feed of two points of view.

268
00:25:04,008 --> 00:25:08,553
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's a live feed going on now, in regard to your experience.

269
00:25:15,061 --> 00:25:15,742
[SPEAKER_01]: And always has been.

270
00:25:36,773 --> 00:25:38,134
[SPEAKER_01]: There were always two points of view.

271
00:25:39,415 --> 00:25:40,236
[SPEAKER_01]: Cannot be different.

272
00:25:41,016 --> 00:25:55,468
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just that that higher one, put it that way, it's usually relegated and overburdened by the concerns of the inferior one and and sort of put second to that one.

273
00:25:56,829 --> 00:26:04,875
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it takes withdrawal from the concerns of the inferior one, through sense restraint, guarding of the sense doors, all of that,

274
00:26:06,287 --> 00:26:08,268
[SPEAKER_01]: To then, shift the weight back.

275
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:11,529
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, obviously, until you eventually see it.

276
00:26:13,850 --> 00:26:17,391
[SPEAKER_01]: And recognize that... Like, as I said, there's a live feed right now.

277
00:26:17,611 --> 00:26:20,612
[SPEAKER_00]: As we speak, we are factually on the planet Earth.

278
00:26:20,992 --> 00:26:22,713
[SPEAKER_01]: As I'm saying, we are on the planet Earth.

279
00:26:22,773 --> 00:26:27,335
[SPEAKER_01]: There is a planet Earth that we inhabit, factually.

280
00:26:29,716 --> 00:26:32,917
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the image of the planet Earth that you have,

281
00:26:34,346 --> 00:26:38,488
[SPEAKER_01]: As an abstract thing, somewhere up there, take it out of space and time.

282
00:26:38,568 --> 00:26:45,912
[SPEAKER_01]: Take it out of up there and see it here, factually living, like the two cameras providing simultaneous light feed.

283
00:26:46,893 --> 00:26:50,735
[SPEAKER_01]: One from the earth, one from what's on earth, more specific.

284
00:27:13,821 --> 00:27:15,082
[SPEAKER_00]: But it needs to be simultaneous.

285
00:27:16,403 --> 00:27:23,127
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like you go and then you start reflecting and thinking about the Earth and then you start applying that here, secondarily.

286
00:27:23,227 --> 00:27:25,148
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, you're probably going to be doing that to some extent.

287
00:27:26,168 --> 00:27:32,552
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have to recognize that this can only be seen rightly if it's simultaneously.

288
00:27:33,493 --> 00:27:35,534
[SPEAKER_01]: Both points of view are simultaneously endured.

289
00:27:42,998 --> 00:27:45,801
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you can't attend to them to the same extent at the same time.

290
00:27:47,804 --> 00:27:49,406
[SPEAKER_01]: One will be actual, another will be peripheral.

291
00:27:49,726 --> 00:27:58,897
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's... whatever is then seen as peripheral, it's not pushed into relegated notion of images and possibilities as second to this.

292
00:27:59,558 --> 00:28:02,361
[SPEAKER_01]: But it's seen real as such, independent of space and time, simultaneous.

293
00:28:05,273 --> 00:28:05,513
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure.

294
00:28:05,613 --> 00:28:06,333
[SPEAKER_01]: Think about it.

295
00:28:06,373 --> 00:28:16,195
[SPEAKER_01]: The great element of Earth is the life feed that's happening now while you sit, walk, talk, eat, sleep.

296
00:28:16,235 --> 00:28:19,816
[SPEAKER_01]: As a necessary basis for you doing all those inferior actions.

297
00:28:23,577 --> 00:28:29,638
[SPEAKER_01]: Air, oxygen, water, heat on that level of the great element... great planet Earth.

298
00:28:36,728 --> 00:28:37,489
[SPEAKER_01]: Peripheral images.

299
00:28:38,489 --> 00:28:40,631
[SPEAKER_01]: But now, understood for what they are.

300
00:28:41,432 --> 00:28:46,415
[SPEAKER_01]: Not assumed as the outside space that I just happen to inhabit and can afford to forget about.

301
00:28:49,337 --> 00:28:49,498
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

302
00:28:50,158 --> 00:28:50,879
[SPEAKER_00]: Completely seen.

303
00:28:53,380 --> 00:28:57,964
[SPEAKER_01]: And it pulls you out, as I said, of that assumption of internal private space as well.

304
00:29:00,085 --> 00:29:01,486
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize, there's nothing private.

305
00:29:01,587 --> 00:29:06,090
[SPEAKER_01]: Even your private internal sense of self and personified space and that nobody's privy to,

306
00:29:07,678 --> 00:29:12,560
[SPEAKER_01]: It's... it's contained within it.

307
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,380
[SPEAKER_01]: Cannot be not there.

308
00:29:15,701 --> 00:29:29,325
[SPEAKER_01]: If you and your form and everything else is on the planet Earth, all of your internal concerns, assumed internally, also have to be within that greater point of view of the greater perspective.

309
00:29:33,767 --> 00:29:34,567
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there's nowhere to hide.

310
00:29:38,003 --> 00:29:58,300
[SPEAKER_01]: And if that greater perspective, that great planet Earth, is seen rightly as subject to destruction, unownable, inconceivable to be owned or controlled, anything that's within it, it's exactly the same.

311
00:29:59,201 --> 00:30:03,144
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when the great external element of Earth and so on, and Mahābhūtas,

312
00:30:06,799 --> 00:30:10,662
[SPEAKER_01]: Start to pervade your internal, personified, me, private.

313
00:30:11,603 --> 00:30:12,304
[SPEAKER_01]: And he's just seeing.

314
00:30:12,344 --> 00:30:18,229
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether it's here, or over there, or even on that highest level, all he sees is form externally.

315
00:30:19,009 --> 00:30:19,730
[SPEAKER_00]: He understands it.

316
00:30:22,192 --> 00:30:27,697
[SPEAKER_01]: So, his understanding of the form externally ceases to be the assumption of the real form behind that.

317
00:30:31,460 --> 00:30:34,903
[SPEAKER_01]: And to the extent that he recognizes it, that's just what he recognized.

318
00:30:49,439 --> 00:30:50,899
[SPEAKER_00]: And he said it in the sutta, wasn't it?

319
00:30:50,999 --> 00:30:52,680
[SPEAKER_01]: I think Aniga quoted that.

320
00:30:55,840 --> 00:31:07,302
[SPEAKER_01]: Whether he thinks about the great mountains or his own body and everything associated with it, he sees there's just form, externally.

321
00:31:12,063 --> 00:31:15,104
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it all becomes external in that sense that it's unownable.

322
00:31:21,583 --> 00:31:28,945
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is the property of Puthujjana's external, what he thinks about.

323
00:31:29,465 --> 00:31:39,529
[SPEAKER_01]: See, the dimension of others, their privates, the privacy that's inaccessible to me, the point of view, what they actually are, that exists outside of me, that is unownable.

324
00:31:43,450 --> 00:31:44,950
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why you fear it, obviously.

325
00:31:45,210 --> 00:31:46,411
[SPEAKER_01]: You can never possess it.

326
00:31:47,211 --> 00:31:50,792
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't see that what you're trying to possess is another image.

327
00:31:52,487 --> 00:32:05,494
[SPEAKER_01]: Neither here nor there, independent of space and time, that you gratuitously allowed the implication that there is the real behind, which is another image, peripheral to that image.

328
00:32:06,594 --> 00:32:07,475
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is none to that.

329
00:32:19,261 --> 00:32:21,842
[SPEAKER_00]: And actually, Sartre did a whole, I think, chapter on that.

330
00:32:23,263 --> 00:32:32,949
[SPEAKER_01]: The being of others always escapes you, always slips through fingers, and it's unownable, and you could dominate them to sadism, or want to be dominated through masochism.

331
00:32:33,009 --> 00:32:41,435
[SPEAKER_01]: I was explaining all these psychological categories, but that domain, that sphere of them, it's completely... always remains inaccessible.

332
00:32:41,475 --> 00:32:49,360
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all these things you try to do, kind of fall short, to possess, to repossess yourself, to possessing others, and whatever you're describing it.

333
00:32:50,744 --> 00:33:02,834
[SPEAKER_01]: But failing to understand that that doesn't matter how big it is, how far, how real it might feel, that they're real in behind, that is real as such as an image first, not as an implication of the outside first.

334
00:33:05,737 --> 00:33:11,922
[SPEAKER_01]: But as I said, that emphasis can only be shifted through repeated contemplation on the basis of right instruction.

335
00:33:13,824 --> 00:33:18,728
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if you have no more reason, no faith to keep repeating the same,

336
00:33:19,932 --> 00:33:26,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Once, it will not undo the perverted emphasis, and you'll dismiss it.

337
00:33:30,437 --> 00:33:34,560
[SPEAKER_01]: But, even if you just approach it logically, how can it not be an image?

338
00:33:35,760 --> 00:33:42,724
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're thinking it, if you're subtly aware of it, how can... well, but there is the real outside behind.

339
00:33:42,924 --> 00:33:45,185
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, how can... how is that not an image now?

340
00:33:58,051 --> 00:33:58,671
[SPEAKER_01]: Simultaneate.

341
00:34:04,632 --> 00:34:05,473
[SPEAKER_01]: Double live feed.

342
00:34:17,315 --> 00:34:18,555
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's also another thing.

343
00:34:19,135 --> 00:34:27,117
[SPEAKER_00]: If the two points of view are always there, simultaneously, one cannot stand without the other.

344
00:34:33,632 --> 00:34:35,473
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

345
00:34:35,513 --> 00:34:40,855
[SPEAKER_01]: The gratuitously elevated, assumed, my one point of view, gets even out.

346
00:34:42,156 --> 00:34:46,237
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is two, to the same extent, there can't be one in charge.

347
00:34:46,677 --> 00:34:52,919
[SPEAKER_01]: Because when one takes charge, it's undermined by the other that's looking at it from the planet Earth live feed.

348
00:34:56,421 --> 00:35:00,062
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you start to, for whatever reason, mystify the planet Earth live feed,

349
00:35:03,020 --> 00:35:12,446
[SPEAKER_01]: And not see the impermanence of that, well, the immediate life feed, arguing over a pot of flowers with somebody, reminds you of the impermanence of that as well.

350
00:35:14,368 --> 00:35:23,734
[SPEAKER_01]: Because if this little pathetic form gets struck here, well, there will be no more perception of the planet Earth life feed either.

